From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeDo <ldileo@digipa.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:48:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RectPacker keeps the order of rectangles of the same size

PackInt and PackIntMulti sort the rectangles by height and width with std::sort, which leaves
rectangles of the same size in an order of its own, not the same in every standard library, so
equal rectangles were placed at positions that depended on the library. Equal sizes are now
ordered by their index.
---
 vcg/space/rect_packer.h | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vcg/space/rect_packer.h b/vcg/space/rect_packer.h
index 0ae90c0..e145bdf 100644
--- a/vcg/space/rect_packer.h
+++ b/vcg/space/rect_packer.h
@@ -397,8 +397,12 @@ public:
     const Point2i &va=v[a];
     const Point2i &vb=v[b];
 
-    return	 (va[1]!=vb[1])?(va[1]>vb[1]):
-                (va[0]>vb[0]);
+    // Rectangles of the same size keep the order they are given in: the sort that uses
+    // this order is not stable, and the standard libraries leave equal elements in different
+    // orders, which would place them at different positions on each platform.
+    if (va[1]!=vb[1]) return va[1]>vb[1];
+    if (va[0]!=vb[0]) return va[0]>vb[0];
+    return a<b;
   }
 };
 
